  "body": "## Progress\n\nAdd the optional native pre-lease Content/NativeWarmup/Abort hook with finite frame and independent-current-QPC budgets. Warmup uses actual SDK SILENT GetBuffer/Release and the existing Start path, preserves original clock/HRESULT receipts, and keeps warmup separate from startup, end guard and callback content. Content latches Live; warmup cannot hide later underflow. Existing callbacks retain their behavior.\n\nRemove the initial 1 GHz conversion restriction using checked integer arithmetic and a fixed 24-step fractional fallback. This converts the independent wait clock; it does not replace original SDK readings. Eighty independent Python integer oracles cover representative frequencies, boundaries and overflow.\n\n## Qualification and retained evidence\n\n- Initial source: four suites/profile in Debug, Release, ASan/UBSan and TSan; 77 lifecycle/19,698 startup checks, zero guarded allocation/free/locks, four actual native-journal interruption boundaries.\n- Final QPC source: four suites/profile in Release 1.14s, ASan/UBSan 11.58s and TSan 17.69s; 157 lifecycle checks including 80 integer oracles, zero guarded violations. No new Debug run is claimed.\n- Final Windows SDK and three test targets compile/link; five modified objects compile without warnings. New native MSVC execution awaits this review. Cross-compilation does not establish installed audio or native SDK playback.\n- Separate packets retain original source identities, selected inputs, executable/object hashes, full logs/configurations/commands and compiler error/warning history. No executables or media are included.\n- Preceding PR139 ordinary protected merge retains four original byte-exact job logs, exact tested tree/base/14 blobs and three original 20-take diagnostic completions. Original Windows failure roots remain unresolved.\n\n## Still required\n\nThe monitor context/binding must consume the startup receipt through this hook and hand off original render clocks once per lease. Explicit auxiliary schema 1.1 migration must retain warmup/readiness/source dispositions and raw-journal binding; schema 1.0 now refuses new evidence instead of dropping it. Ten refusal cases preserve pending state and permit later valid finalization.\n\nNative factory remains disabled. Native/installed Linux+Windows, professional latency, EQ/mixing, alignment and punch/loop remain open. No GUI, VM, audio-route, driver, dependency or branch-protection changes. Full M2\u2013M11/F/Q/C/N/X004/X005/all-Europe goal remains incomplete.\n",
